  "strategy": "Approach and rationale\nOur goal is to find a step function h: [0,2] \u2192 [0,1] withintegral 1 that minimizes the maximum overlap integral C_5, which is defined as the maximum over all shifts k of the integral of h(x) * (1 - h(x+k)) dx, normalized by dx=2.0/n_points. This is a non-convex optimization problem because of the product terms and the shift operation. The current record value is approximately 0.38085, and the \u00d6zcanuer approach involves using a multi-resolution strategy with coarse-to-fine optimization to fully explore the solution space and avoid local optima. The key innovation is combining global optimization (Differential Evolution) with local refinement (SLSQP) at different discretization levels.\n\nThe main bottlenecks are:\n- Local optima from gradient-based methods\n- High dimensionality when using dense grids (up to 560 points)\n- Expensive gradient computations\n\nThe approach overcomes these by:\n1. Using Differential Evolution for global exploration\n2. Switching to SLSQP for local refinement where gradients are accurate\n3. Progressive resolution refinement from 70 to potential 840 points\n4. Careful time budgeting to balance depth and resolution\n\nThe expected improvement comes from:\n- Coverage of a wider solution space compared to random/local search\n- Handling constraints by projection and repair\n- Progressive validation with exact integral preservation\n\nMathematical specification\nWe minimize C_5=max_k \u222b h(x)(1-h(x+k)) dx subject to:\n0 \u2264 h_i \u2264 1 for all i\n\u2211h_i \u00b7 dx = 1 (integral=1)\n\nRepresentation: Discrete function values h_i at points x_i = i\u00b7dx for i=0,...,n-1\nVariable space: n-dimensional [0,1]^n with linear constraint\n\nObjective: The correlation metric computed as:\n   C_5 = (2.0/n) \u00b7 max_l  [sum_{k} h_k \u00b7 (1-h_{k+l})]   for l in [-n+1, n-1]\n\nImplementation procedure\n1. Setting up\n   a. Collect input parameters:\n      - Time budget (budget_s)\n      - Random seed\n      - Global parent solution (if available)\n      - Maximum level of resolution (starts at 70 points)\n\n   b. Precompute:\n      - dx factor = 2.0/n_points\n      - Target sum per level: n_points=140/200/700\u2192 sum_adjust= target=sum(h)/dx=1\n      - Dimensions: initialize from parent or random\n\n2. Initial state\n   a. If parent solution exists at 70 points:\n        n=70, start with parent\n   b Else:\n        Generate random candidate:\n          Sum = cumulative_sum = 350.0\n          Generate vector: rng.random(size=n) where sum(u)=350\n\n   c. Repair/fix constraints (clip and scale)\n\n3. Optimization loop\n   For level in [min_level, max_level] to [70, 350, 560, ...]:\n   a. Set n_points (target resolution)\n   b. Prepare bounds: [(0,1)] * n_points\n   c. Compute target_sum = ceil(0.5/dx) \u2248 n//2\n   d. Repair initial candidates:\n        parent_candidates = [initial_parent] if available\n        random_candidates + repair(sum_candidates)\n\n   e. Use Differential Evolution:\n      - Objective: maximize the log-sum of exponential potentials (temperature-annealed)\n      - Bounds: defined clip to [0,1]\n      - Max. evaluations: floor(budget_level)\n\n   f. If progress threshold reached beyond current best:\n        Advance to next level and initialize from the best solution\n\n   g. Use SLSQP for local refinement:\n      - Fix current best candidates to ensure sum constraints\n      - Temperature with penalty: start at T=50 then decrease\n      - Gradient computation via soft_max_grad function\n      - Stop when improvement below 1e-5 or max_iter reached\n\n4. Validation\n   After each candidate generation:\n   - Repair if needed\n   - Recompute C_5 with exact correlation (mode=\"full\")\n   - Record improvement (-log(transform_scores))\n\n5. Advancement conditions\n   - BudgetExpired: return best candidate\n   - Timeout on current level: silence and keep best candidate\n   - No improvement in X iterations: move up level\n   - Time_remaining < ceil(time per level)\n\nSearch choices and variations\n1. Temperature-based repair:\n   range T from 5-500 for soft_max function\n2. Candidate generation diversity:\n   Start patterns: parent initialized, random uniform, sinusoidal modulation\n   Temperature: cyclic through values [5,10,20,40,60]\n3. Population management:\n   - Start population: level_type=200\n   - Quorum threshold for advancing to higher level\n   - Mutation strategy: coordinated across all levels\n\nCompute budget and robustness\n1. Level time per resolution d: 20*d/100 seconds budget, limiting to 2 levels (\u223c800 points)\n2. Memory: feasible for up to 560 points\n3. Repairs:\n   - Clip bounds with log-sum penalty avoidance\n   - Repair constraint with update_rate=0.2\n   - Gradient clipping at max norm=1e4\n\nValidation and return contract\n1. Ensure outputs satisfy:\n   - Sum(h) = n/2.0 (within 1e-6)\n   - Each h[i] in [0,1]\n   - Computed C_5 from np.correlate\n\n2. Validation steps:\n   - Check definite C_5 score with exact normalization\n   - Repair with adaptive momentum if sum constraint not met\n   - Reject candidates that violate [0,1] after multiple repairs\n\n3. Main output:\n   (h_vectors, c5_bound, n_points)\n\n   where h_vectors is the most promising solution found",
